    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0396" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15307: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-19T14:00:00+07:00">March 19, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>487. Drumright in telegram from Sian March 18 states report current there that
                    Communists have recently transferred many troops <pb facs="0397" n="383"
                        xml:id="pg383"/> back to occupied North China from Yenan because of food
                    shortage North Shensi.</p>
                <p>Informed Central Government official states Lin Pai-hsu, chairman Yenan border
                    government, left Yenan March 14 enroute Chungking for discussion Kmt–Communist
                    reactions (Embassy’s 258, February 8, 3 p.m.) and that situation is
                    improving.</p>
                <p>It is reliably reported foreign correspondents will leave Chungking enroute
                    Communist area about April 2 (Embassy’s 456, March 11 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >10</hi>], 4 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m.), although no public
                    announcement yet made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
